            <div xml:id="d257">

                <pb facs="0618" n="590" xml:id="pg590"/>

                <head>257. Memorandum From the Duty Officer in the White House
                        Situation Room to the President<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d257-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1964-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                        1964.</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. President: <list>
                        <label>1.</label>
                        <item>Early this morning the USS
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Maddox</hi> was attacked by three DRV
                            PT boats while on patrol approximately 30
                            miles off the North Vietnamese coast in the Gulf of Tonkin.</item>
                        <label>2.</label>
                        <item>The Captain of the <hi rendition="#italic">Maddox</hi> returned the
                            fire with 5-inch guns and requested air support from the carrier <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Ticonderoga</hi> on station nearby in connection
                            with reconnaissance flights in that area.</item>
                        <label>3.</label>
                        <item><hi rendition="#italic">Ticonderoga</hi> jets arrived shortly and made
                            strafing attacks on the PT boats
                            resulting in one enemy boat dead in the water, two others damaged and
                            turned tail for home.</item>
                        <label>4.</label>
                        <item>The <hi rendition="#italic">Maddox</hi> reports no personnel or
                            material damages.</item>
                        <label>5.</label>
                        <item>Messrs. Rusk and McNamara have been informed of the
                            incident and present plans are to release a press statement later today
                            either from Washington or Saigon.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d257-f2"/></item>
                        <label>6.</label>
                        <item>Additional details on the <hi rendition="#italic">Maddox</hi>
                            encounter will be available later today.</item>
                    </list></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d257-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d257-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Johnson Library, National Security File, Vietnam Country File, Operation
                    Pierce Arrow. No classification marking. Printed in part in Johnson, Vantage
                    Point, p. 112. The President recalled that this memorandum was sent to him in
                    his bedroom. Since his Daily Diary shows breakfast at 9 a.m., he must have
                    received it before that time.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d257-f2" n="2" xml:id="d257-f2-content">
                <p>For text of the statement, released at 10:15 a.m., see Goulden, <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Truth,</hi> p. 23.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
